11604	{"artifactId":"LLD-f52996c2709dba81-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-f52996c2709dba81-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-16T09:09:46.329Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The four derived acceptance criteria (repo-relative label, page script marks and posts, pane forwards only from its own frame, grammar shared with the chat page) are each designed. Nothing outside the stated scope is built: alternative a2's IR and builder changes are rejected and not built.","evidence":"There is no upstream SPEC or HLD (standalone), so the intent is the Story's focus. Sections 2.1 to 2.4 design one element per ac: buildCallSequenceIR/frameLabel for ac1, CODE_REF_SCRIPT for ac2, rvFrameMessage for ac3, and the pin test for ac4. Section 7.2 keeps companion builders and the IR unchanged, and section 3 limits the IR change to the label text. [files: src/docgen/extract/call-sequence.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today frameLabel labels a call frame with only the base name of its file and the line, and makeExtract, which has scope.repoRoot, is the builder's only production caller.","evidence":"call-sequence.ts:86-88: `return `${f.name} (${basename(f.file)}:${f.startLine})`;`. The only production call is line 217, `return ok(buildCallSequenceIR(walk, revision, desc));`, inside makeExtract, where `scope.repoRoot` is in hand (line 207). The other callers are in __tests__/call-sequence.test.ts. [files: src/docgen/extract/call-sequence.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The pane's companion frame is sandboxed with allow-scripts only and gets the page as srcdoc. It inherits the pane's CSP, so a script in it runs only with the pane's nonce.","evidence":"docs-review-panel.ts:2078-2079: `f.setAttribute('sandbox','allow-scripts');... f.setAttribute('srcdoc',m.html)`. The pane's CSP at line 1960 is `script-src 'nonce-${nonce}'`, and the comment at 2072-2073 says the frame inherits it. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The companion pan/zoom viewport captures the pointer on pointerdown and handles drag, wheel and double-click zoom. A click's target is therefore the viewport, so the script has to record the element at pointerdown.","evidence":"panzoom.js:97-102: the pointerdown listener on vp calls `vp.setPointerCapture(ev.pointerId)`. Lines 90 and 116 handle wheel and dblclick zoom on vp. None of these handlers calls stopPropagation, so a capture-phase document listener sees pointerdown first, as the design assumes. [files: src/assets/artifacts/companion/panzoom.js]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The host's openCodeRef refuses a non-string path or a '..' segment and resolves the path inside the workspace root, logging 'a code reference was not opened' when it cannot.","evidence":"link-opener.ts:62-69: `if (typeof path !== 'string' || path.split(/[\\\\/]/).includes('..'))` gives a warning, then `resolveWithin(root, path, fs)`. When that returns undefined it logs `a code reference was not opened: ... is not a file inside the workspace`. The line is clamped at 71. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-opener.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused chat grammar CREF_EXT/CREF_CORE exists with the stated shape (relative path, optional :N, :N-M, :N:C). It allows a bare file name, which the new script intentionally narrows by requiring a '/'.","evidence":"link-markup.ts:20-21: `CREF_CORE='((?:[A-Za-z0-9_.@-]+/)*[A-Za-z0-9_@-][A-Za-z0-9_.@-]*\\\\.(?:'+CREF_EXT+'))(?::(\\\\d+)(?:-\\\\d+)?(?::\\\\d+)?)?'`. The directory group is `*` (zero or more), so a bare name matches, as the design's edge-case table says. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-markup.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CODE_REF_SCRIPT and rvFrameMessage are new. No page script that posts a clicked reference and no frame-message handler exist today, and the existing open-code-ref payload is reused unchanged.","evidence":"A grep for 'insrc-open-code-ref' and rvFrameMessage finds nothing. The pane's only window message listener (docs-review-panel.ts:2224-2228) reads `e.data.payload` and handles docs-list, docs-content, docs-decision-result and docs-companion. The open-code-ref shape is in protocol.ts:306, and the host case is at docs-review-panel.ts:2354. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Putting CODE_REF_SCRIPT in a standalone src/docgen/render/code-ref-script.ts avoids an import cycle between the companion shell and the docgen shells.","evidence":"companion/shell.ts:30 already imports `docgenAssetDir` from '../../../docgen/render/shell.js', and fallback.ts:24-25 forbids importing from shell.ts. A leaf module imported by all three adds no cycle. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/companion/shell.ts, src/docgen/render/fallback.ts, src/docgen/render/shell.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Both docgen page shells (Mermaid buildHtml and assembleFallbackShell) and the companion renderCompanionPage are the full set of page builders that need the script. The Mermaid shells can run it after mermaid.run resolves, and the fallback can run it at load.","evidence":"shell.ts:204-216: the init does `await mermaid.run(...)` inside an async IIFE with a catch that writes #docgen-error. fallback.ts:216-224 has no Mermaid; the SVG is inline at 240. companion/shell.ts:160-167 calls `mermaid.run(...).then(...)` with a catch, and the HTML visual calls init with fitOnLoad (158). These three are the only HTML page assemblers in src/docgen/render and the companion folder. [files: src/docgen/render/shell.ts, src/docgen/render/fallback.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/shell.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding an optional fourth parameter repoRoot to buildCallSequenceIR leaves the existing 3-argument test callers valid.","evidence":"call-sequence.test.ts calls `buildCallSequenceIR(walk, 'rev1', 'scope')` and similar at lines 52, 71, 85, 99, 109, 167 and 179. With an optional fourth parameter these still type-check, and frameLabel keeps its base-name output when the root is absent. [files: src/docgen/extract/__tests__/call-sequence.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Only the call-frame label text changes. Node ids, edge ids and citations are built independently of the label, so stored citations still resolve.","evidence":"call-sequence.ts:102-107: node `id: f.entityId`, `citation: { entityId: f.entityId }`. Edge ids at 110 are built from step indices and entity ids, and only `label: frameLabel(f)` changes. Callees can come from outside the repo root (the CALLS neighbours in call-graph-reader.ts:55-71 are not repo-filtered), and the design's base-name fallback covers that case. [files: src/docgen/extract/call-sequence.ts, src/docgen/extract/call-graph-reader.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A new inline script tag in a companion page gets the pane's nonce from the host (this answers open question 2), so it runs in the frame rather than being silently blocked by the CSP.","evidence":"docs-review-panel.ts:2437-2438: `stampScriptNonce` replaces `/<script\\b(?![^>]*\\bnonce\\s*=)/gi` with `<script nonce=...>`, so every script tag without a nonce gets one. It is applied to every companion text at line 1696, `html = stampScriptNonce(text, shellNonce)`. Open question 2 can be closed as confirmed. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"Close open question 2 as confirmed (stampScriptNonce stamps every un-nonced script).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A flat { type: 'insrc-open-code-ref' } message from the frame cannot be confused with a host message by the pane's existing listener, and a message from another window is ignored by comparing e.source with the current frame.","evidence":"The existing listener at docs-review-panel.ts:2224 does `var m=e.data&&e.data.payload;if(!m)return;`, so a flat frame message is a no-op there. rvDropFrame (2059) removes the old frame on every tab change and rvCompanion (2078) creates a new one. The design must therefore compare against the frame currently in frameHostEl, which is what its precondition states. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1 to ac4 maps to named tests. The contract test pinning the script's grammar to the plugin's CREF_EXT/CREF_CORE can live in the root src test tree, because root tests already read vscode-plugin source files.","evidence":"Section 5 maps every ac to tests. Root tests already read plugin files: src/mcp/__tests__/review-rule-text.test.ts:25 reads `vscode-plugin/assets/steering-block.md`, and src/config/__tests__/retired-roles.test.ts:48 reads `vscode-plugin/package.json`. A pin test that reads link-markup.ts as text is feasible. Minor: the code-ref-script tests are placed under src/workflow/artifacts/companion/__tests__ although the module lives in src/docgen/render; this does not block. [files: src/mcp/__tests__/review-rule-text.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/link-markup.ts]","action":"Optionally place the code-ref-script tests under src/docgen/render/__tests__ beside the module.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-16T09:09:46.329Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
